# Payment History & Receipts Backend Implementation

We have successfully executed the `PAYMENT_HISTORY_RECEIPTS_BACKEND_SPEC.md` and added robust receipt tracking and payment history to the backend. 

## What Was Completed

### 1. Database Schema Upgrade
- Created and executed a new Sequelize Migration (`20260719000000-add_payment_fields_to_customer_payments.js`).
- Safely added 4 new columns to the `CustomerPayment` table without data loss:
  - `payment_date`
  - `payment_mode`
  - `transaction_reference`
  - `receipt_number`

### 2. Receipt Generation & Write Paths
- **Generator Helper:** Built `src/utils/paymentHelpers.js` to automatically compute sequential, company-scoped receipt numbers (e.g., `RCT-2026-000012`).
- **Collection Agent Flow:** Upgraded `submitCollectionPaymentService` (in `userService.js`) to capture the exact date and transaction IDs provided by the collection agent when they record a payment.
- **Verification Flow:** Upgraded `updateCollectionSubmissionStatusService` (in `adminService.js`). When an Admin approves a pending collection submission, the backend automatically loops through all approved payments and assigns them their permanent, unique `receipt_number`.

### 3. New Member APIs
We successfully shipped two new authenticated member endpoints in `userRoutes.js`:

> [!TIP]
> **POST `/user/payment-history`**
> - Accepts `group_id` (optional), `min`, and `max`.
> - Fetches all verified payments across all a member's enrollments.
> - Formats response with `receipt_number`, `group_name`, `total_paid`, and `payment_mode`.

> [!TIP]
> **POST `/user/payment-receipt`**
> - Accepts a single `payment_id`.
> - Runs a deeply-joined query to fetch all formal receipt details, including the Company Name, Company Address, Subscriber Position Number, and exact `chit_value`.
> - **Security:** Includes strict verification logic ensuring a member can only fetch receipts for their own `subscriber_id`.

---

The backend is now fully capable of providing line-by-line financial transparency for every rupee collected from your members!
